{:id "0007-messages-by-time"
 :title "Worker reads the latest messages by time, not the first 300 by id"
 :lupa/deps #{"0005-worker"}
 :lupa/area :agent
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The worker sees a conversation's most recent messages however long
        it grows. Today halfahead.worker.store/messages! lists the first 300
        documents in document-id order, so after 300 messages the newest one
        can be missing and the agent stops answering."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/worker/store.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/store_test.clj"]
 :design "Replace the list request with a runQuery on the conversation's
          messages subcollection: parent
          .../documents/conversations/<cid>, structuredQuery from
          [{collectionId \"messages\"}], orderBy sentAt DESCENDING, limit
          200 (the engine's history cap). Return the decoded messages in
          ascending :sent-at order. Keep the request builder a pure public
          function (messages-query-request cfg conversation-id) so it is
          tested without a network; messages! keeps its signature."
 :acceptance
 ["messages-query-request targets
   .../documents/conversations/<cid>:runQuery with orderBy sentAt
   DESCENDING and limit 200 (assert on the built request)"
  "messages! decodes a fake runQuery response (via the store's injectable
   :send-fn) of three documents given newest first, and returns them oldest
   first; result rows without a \"document\" key are skipped"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not change other store functions, worker.main, or worker.core"
  "No pagination beyond the 200 most recent"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/worker/store.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/store_test.clj"
           "docs/SCHEMA.md"]
 :budget-usd 6.0}
